<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="ID-1208-00000759" xml:lang="en-us" class="- topic/topic task/task "><title class="- topic/title ">Reviewing a PC’s TCP/IP changes</title><!--This topic is shared by docJ8Startup and docJ9Startup.--><shortdesc class="- topic/shortdesc ">You configure a PC’s TCP/IP settings using Windows. <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/Workbench" class="- topic/keyword "/>  records TCP/IP before and after the change values in an <filepath class="+ topic/ph sw-d/filepath ">ipchanges.bog</filepath> file. If necessary, you can review these
changes.</shortdesc><prolog class="- topic/prolog "><metadata class="- topic/metadata "><keywords class="- topic/keywords "><indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">TCP/IP changes<indexterm class="- topic/indexterm ">reviewing
for a PC</indexterm></indexterm></keywords><prodinfo class="- topic/prodinfo "><prodname class="- topic/prodname "><keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/niagara" conref="../reuse/WH_SoftwareVariables_Tridium_N4_0000009934.dita#WHSoftwareVariablesTridium-9A3264AE/niagara" class="- topic/keyword "/></prodname><vrmlist class="- topic/vrmlist "><vrm version="4.1" class="- topic/vrm "/></vrmlist></prodinfo></metadata></prolog><taskbody class="- topic/body task/taskbody "><prereq class="- topic/section task/prereq ">You are working in <keyword conkeyref="wh_variables_n4/Workbench" class="- topic/keyword "/>  with a connection to your PC.</prereq><steps class="- topic/ol task/steps "><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">In the Nav tree, expand <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">My Host</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">My File System</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">User Home</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">ipchanges.bog</uicontrol></menucascade>.</cmd><info class="- topic/itemgroup task/info "><p class="- topic/p ">Child folders are date-named using the following convention:</p><p class="- topic/p ">&lt;<userinput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/userinput ">yyyymmddhhmmss</userinput>&gt;, where the variable
name contains year, month, day, hours, minutes, seconds; for example, <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">d20250113153640</systemoutput> for 2025 Jan 13 3:36pm and 40 seconds.</p></info></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">To expand a folder, right-click and select <menucascade class="+ topic/ph ui-d/menucascade "><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Views</uicontrol><uicontrol class="+ topic/ph ui-d/uicontrol ">Property Sheet</uicontrol></menucascade>. </cmd><stepresult class="- topic/itemgroup task/stepresult ">The <wintitle class="+ topic/keyword ui-d/wintitle ">Property Sheet</wintitle> for the folder
opens.<p class="- topic/p ">The included decoded <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">modTime</parmname> value is easier to read. For example, <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">13-Jan-2024 03:36 PM EST</systemoutput> instead of <systemoutput class="+ topic/ph sw-d/systemoutput ">d20150113153640</systemoutput>).</p><?Pub Caret 81?><p class="- topic/p ">Under each
folder are two properties:</p><ul class="- topic/ul "><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "><parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">priorValue</parmname> reports the TCP/IP settings
that existed before the change.</p></li><li class="- topic/li "><p class="- topic/p "><parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">newValue</parmname> reports the TCP/IP settings that
existed after the change.</p></li></ul></stepresult></step><step class="- topic/li task/step "><cmd class="- topic/ph task/cmd ">Expand a <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">priorValue</parmname> or <parmname class="+ topic/keyword pr-d/parmname ">newValue</parmname> to see the reported settings.</cmd></step></steps></taskbody></task>